                    "Fiduciary Audit Logging & OpenTelemetry SIEM Integration guarantees end-to-end regulatory defensibility. Every intercepted completion automatically emits a cryptographically signed Common Event Format (CEF) or Open Cybersecurity Schema Framework (OCSF) event to enterprise governance repositories (such as Splunk, Datadog, or Microsoft Sentinel). These audit events document the originating model version, prompt hash, exact character offsets of flagged violations, anonymized PII tokens, and the precise fallback message delivered to the user. When internal risk committees or external regulatory auditors inspect the enterprise AI infrastructure, these immutable audit trails provide definitive mathematical proof of proactive risk mitigation.",
                    "In this final masterclass implementation, we construct the complete Enterprise Output Guardrail Firewall in pure standard Python. We execute an end-to-end defense transaction on hazardous financial output containing both unmasked PII and an illegal return guarantee, demonstrate instantaneous fallback substitution, verify compliant transaction release, and confer the CEAGA credential."
